  str_draw_card_pool_detail_sub_desc20052_1 = [[
This limited-time recruitment opens periodically, and Special Star Flares can be used to recruit from it. After the limited-time recruitment update, a 5-Star Aurorian is guaranteed within your first 10 recruitments.

The initial probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian from this recruitment is <color=#ffbb00>2%</color>. If you fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian after 50 recruitments in a row, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian on your next recruitment attempt will increase from <color=#ffbb00>2%</color> to <color=#ffbb00>4.5%</color>. If you still fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian on your next recruitment attempt will increase from <color=#ffbb00>4.5%</color> to <color=#ffbb00>7%</color>, and so on. Whenever you fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will increase by <color=#ffbb00>2.5%</color> until it reaches <color=#ffbb00>100%</color>. After obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will be reset to <color=#ffbb00>2%</color>.

All limited-time recruitments follow the above rules. This means that, in all limited-time recruitments, if you fail to obtain a 6-Star Aurorian, your probability of obtaining one will accumulate in your next recruitment attempts. This accumulated probability will not be cleared at the end of the limited-time recruitment and will be carried over to the next limited-time recruitment. If multiple limited-time recruitments are active simultaneously, this probability will accumulate and apply to each of them collectively. Whenever you obtain a 6-Star Aurorian from any limited-time recruitment, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will be reset to <color=#ffbb00>2%</color>.

Limited-time recruitments have a guarantee mechanism. If the 6-star Aurorian obtained <color=#ffbb00>2</color> times in a row is not the 6-star Aurorian with increased probability in this recruitment, then the next 6-star Aurorian obtained through this recruitment will <color=#ffbb00>definitely</color> be the 6-star Aurorian with increased probability. Each time a 6-star Aurorian with increased probability is obtained, the guarantee mechanism will be reset and recalculated. This accumulated probability will not be cleared at the end of the limited-time recruitment, and will be carried over to the next limited-time recruitment. If multiple limited-time recruitments are active at the same time, they will share this guaranteed mechanism. Thus, any limited-time recruitment attempt during the same period will also cause the guaranteed mechanism to be calculated and reset. The 6-star Aurorian obtained when the guarantee mechanism is triggered will be based on the limited-time recruitment attempted.

Please note that limited-time recruitment's increased probability and guarantee mechanism are independent of other types of recruitments' increased probability and guarantee mechanisms. Probability increases and guarantee mechanisms only apply within the respective recruitment pools.

