The Class Targeted Recruitment is limited-time special recruitment. There are a total of 4 recruitment pools that will be available over 4 weeks, with 1 targeted recruitment each week, respectively:
Converter (Week 1): September 29 to October 6
Sniper (Week 2): October 6 to October 13
Detonator (Week 3): October 13 to October 20
Supporter (Week 4): October 20 to October 27

This recruitment is targeted recruitment for Supporters, which means you will only get Supporters from this recruitment pool. You can use Star Flares to recruit from it and the first 10 recruitments are guaranteed to include one 5-Star Supporter Aurorian.

The probability of obtaining characters of different ratings in the recruitment will be the same as in regular recruitment. For specifics, please refer to Aurorian Obtaining Chance Info.

The initial probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian from this recruitment is 2%. If you fail to obtain a 6-Star Aurorian after 50 attempts in a row, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian on your next recruitment attempt will increase from 2% to 4.5%. If you fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian on this recruitment attempt, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian on your next recruitment attempt will increase from 4.5% to 7%, and so on. Whenever you fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will increase by 2.5% until it reaches 100% and guarantees a 6-Star Aurorian. After obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will be reset to 2%.

Note: In this Class Targeted Recruitment (all 4 targeted recruitments from September 29 to October 27), if you failed to obtain a 6-star Aurorian in a Class Targeted Recruitment pool, your accumulated attempts will carry over to the next Class Targeted Recruitment pool. However, the increased probability for the targeted recruitments does not carry over to any other recruitment pools in the same period nor to any future recruitments.]],
