  str_draw_card_pool_detail_title_90001 = "Mystery Hero Collection Recruitment Info",
  str_draw_card_pool_detail_sub_desc90001_1 = [[
The Collection Recruitment will be available for the specified period, and you can use Star Flares to recruit from it. The first 6-Star Aurorian you get from this recruitment is guaranteed to be a 6-Star Aurorian from the Mainstay Recruitment (the Farewell, My "Wonderland" version) that you don't already own:
<color=#ffbb00>Raphael, Uriel, Gabriel, Michael, Eicy, Jona, Charon, Victoria, Sharona, Sariel, Connolly, Nikinis, Migard, Irridon, Gronru, Wrath, Carleen, Sinsa, Eve, Hiiro, Beryl, Fleur, Smokey, Gram, Revy, Paloma, Luke, Bethel, Hedy, Novio, Siobhan, Ruby, Florine, Rinne, Yao, Amemori, Azure, Lenore, Giles, Barton: Deft Blades, Nina, Carleen: Smoldering Soul, Fia, Jeno</color>

The rules of the Collection Recruitment are as follows:

- A 5-Star Aurorian is guaranteed within your first 10 recruitments.
- 6-Star Aurorians, 5-Star Aurorians, and 4-Star Aurorians recruited from this pool will be from the Farewell, My "Wonderland" version of the Mainstay Recruitment.
- <color=#ffbb00>The first 6-Star Aurorian you get from the Collection Recruitment will be an Aurorian from the available pool that you don't already have. If you already have all the 6-Star Aurorians in the pool, the first 6-Star Aurorian you recruit from the pool will be one of the available 6-Star Aurorians at random.</color>
- 6-star Aurorian probability increase mechanism: The initial probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian from this recruitment is <color=#ffbb00>2%</color>. If you fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian after <color=#ffbb00>50</color> recruitments in a row, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian on your next recruitment attempt will increase from <color=#ffbb00>2%</color> to <color=#ffbb00>4.5%</color>. If you still fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian on your next recruitment attempt will increase from <color=#ffbb00>4.5%</color> to <color=#ffbb00>7%</color>, and so on. Whenever you fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will increase by <color=#ffbb00>2.5%</color> until it reaches <color=#ffbb00>100%</color>. After obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will be reset to <color=#ffbb00>2%</color>
Note:
 - The increased probability mechanism of the Collection Recruitment is independent of other types of recruitments' increased probability mechanisms. The increased probability mechanism of this exclusive recruitment is only valid during this period and will not be carried over to any future rounds of the Collection Recruitment.
 - This recruitment does not affect the guarantee mechanisms of other recruitments.]],
