  str_draw_card_pool_name_60008 = "Twilight Symphony Exclusive Recruitment",
  str_draw_card_pool_title_60008_1 = "Twilight Symphony",
  str_draw_card_pool_title_60008_2 = "Increased chance of recruiting Wrath: Proud Fervor and Joselyne during the event period!",
  str_draw_card_pool_detail_title_60008 = "Twilight Symphony Exclusive Recruitment Info",
  str_draw_card_pool_detail_sub_desc60008_1 = [[
This exclusive recruitment will be available for a limited time during the specified period. Special Star Flares can be used to recruit from this pool, which includes a 6-star exclusive Aurorian <color=#ffbb00>Wrath: Proud Fervor</color> and a 5-star non-exclusive Aurorian <color=#ffbb00>Joselyne</color>. When recruiting a 6-star Aurorian, you will have a 50% chance of recruiting Wrath: Proud Fervor. When recruiting a 5-star Aurorian, you will have a 25% chance of recruiting Joselyne. These 2 Aurorians will not be present in other recruitments.

The exclusive recruitment rules are as follows:

- A 5-star Aurorian is guaranteed within your first 10 recruitments.

- This Aurorian can only be recruited from the <color=#ffbb00>exclusive recruitment</color> and will not be obtainable from other recruitments. The exclusive Aurorian <color=#ffbb00>Wrath: Proud Fervor</color> will not be available by any other method after this recruitment ends, until at least <color=#ffbb00>29 February, 2024</color>. Please refer to official announcements for future availability details after this recruitment ends.

- Joselyne is a non-exclusive 5-star Aurorian. After the Twilight Symphony Exclusive Recruitment, Joselyne will be added to the Mainstay Recruitment and all limited-time recruitments afterward through updates. Aurorians obtainable from the Mainstay Recruitment and all following limited-time recruitments will have the same chance of appearing as other non-event Aurorians of the same rating.

- 6-star Aurorian probability increase mechanism: The initial probability of obtaining a 6-star Aurorian from this recruitment is <color=#ffbb00>2%</color>. If you fail to recruit a 6-star Aurorian after <color=#ffbb00>50</color> recruitments in a row, the probability of obtaining a 6-star Aurorian on your next recruitment attempt will increase from <color=#ffbb00>2%</color> to <color=#ffbb00>4.5%</color>. If you still fail to recruit a 6-star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-star Aurorian on your next recruitment attempt will increase from <color=#ffbb00>4.5%</color> to <color=#ffbb00>7%</color>, and so on. Whenever you fail to recruit a 6-star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will increase by <color=#ffbb00>2.5%</color> until it reaches <color=#ffbb00>100%</color>. After obtaining a 6-star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-star Aurorian will be reset to <color=#ffbb00>2%</color>.

- Guarantee Mechanism: If the 6-star Aurorian featured in this exclusive recruitment is not obtained within <color=#ffbb00>2</color> consecutive attempts, then the next 6-star Aurorian obtained through this recruitment is <color=#ffbb00>guaranteed</color> to be the featured 6-star Aurorian. Each time the featured 6-star Aurorian is obtained, the guarantee mechanism will be reset and recalculated.

Note: This exclusive recruitment's increased probability and guarantee mechanisms are independent of other types of recruitment's increased probability and guarantee mechanisms. Twilight Symphony's increased probability and guarantee mechanisms are only valid during this period and will not be carried over to the next exclusive recruitment.]],
