  str_draw_card_pool_detail_sub_desc50067_1 = [[
This is a limited-time recommended recruitment, where you can use Star Flares for recruitment. In this recruitment, you are guaranteed to get at least one 5-Star Aurorian within your first 10 recruitments.

In the Recommendation Recruitment, the initial probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian is <color=#ffbb00>2%</color>. If you fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian after 50 recruitments in a row, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian on your next recruitment attempt will increase from <color=#ffbb00>2%</color> to <color=#ffbb00>4.5%</color>. If you still fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian on your next recruitment attempt will increase from <color=#ffbb00>4.5%</color> to <color=#ffbb00>7%</color>, and so on. Whenever you fail to recruit a 6-Star Aurorian, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will increase by <color=#ffbb00>2.5%</color> until it reaches <color=#ffbb00>100%</color>, after which, you will <color=#ffbb00>definitely</color> receive a 6-Star Aurorian.

After obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian, the increased probability will become invalid, and the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will be reset to <color=#ffbb00>2%</color>.

In all recommendation recruitments, if you fail to obtain a 6-Star Aurorian, your probability of obtaining one will accumulate. All recommendation recruitments follow the above rules. Whenever you obtain a 6-Star Aurorian from any recommendation recruitment, the probability of obtaining a 6-Star Aurorian will be reset to <color=#ffbb00>2%</color>.

This recruitment has a guarantee mechanism. If the 6-star Aurorian obtained <color=#ffbb00>2</color> times in a row is not the 6-star Aurorian with increased probability in this recruitment, then the next 6-star Aurorian obtained through this recruitment will <color=#ffbb00>definitely</color> be the Aurorian with increased probability in this recruitment. Each time a 6-star Aurorian with increased probability is obtained, the guarantee mechanism will be reset and recalculated.

This limited-time recruitment uses the Wishlist system. After the wishlist is applied, <color=#ffbb00>any 6-Star Aurorians you obtain are guaranteed to be one from your wishlist</color>.
The Wishlist includes a total of 5 Aurorians: one of them is the Rate-Up Aurorian for this recruitment, Maya, who cannot be changed and takes up a 50% chance of obtaining 6-Star Aurorians. The remaining 4 Aurorians need to be set by the Navigator, with one Aurorian from each element. After setting, each Aurorian will take up a 12.5% chance of obtaining 6-Star Aurorians.
The Wishlist only takes effect after all four elemental Aurorians are set. That is, if no Aurorians are selected or only some are selected for the Wishlist, the Wishlist will not take effect, and Aurorians will still be obtained according to the original probability in the recruitment.
In the recruitment, the overall probability of obtaining a 6-star Aurorian is not affected by the Wishlist mechanism, and mechanisms such as rate-up and guarantees still apply.]],
